// REJECTS: Unexpected token '~mainMapping'. Valid alternatives: ['Views']
//
// An AggregationAware class mapping is `Views: [ ... ] , ~mainMapping: <parser> { ... }` in
// that order. The main mapping -- the detail table, the thing the class really is -- comes
// LAST, after the list of pre-aggregated views that are only an optimisation.
//
// So the natural reading order is the illegal one, and unlike most of this grammar the two
// parts are separated by a COMMA, which reads like a set rather than a sequence. A rewrite
// that parses the body as comma-separated named fields accepts either order.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::MainMappingFirst
(
   *fixture::neg::TradeFact: AggregationAware
   {
      ~mainMapping: Relational
      {
         ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db] TRADE
         bookId: [fixture::neg::Db] TRADE.BOOK_ID
      },
      Views:
      [
         (
            ~modelOperation:
            {
               ~canAggregate false,
               ~groupByFunctions
               (
                  $this.bookId
               ),
               ~aggregateValues
               (
                  ( ~mapFn: $this.notional, ~aggregateFn: $mapped->sum() )
               )
            },
            ~aggregateMapping: Relational
            {
               ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db] TRADE_BY_BOOK
               bookId: [fixture::neg::Db] TRADE_BY_BOOK.BOOK_ID
            }
         )
      ]
   }
)
